WEBVTT

00:00:03.399 --> 00:00:10.894
Who is traveling?. Travel alone or choose that you have company. The route adapts to the people traveling. This example keeps one traveler.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:28.557
Your starting point is optional. Add your origin, departure date and time if known. Transport can remain undecided. If you do not have these details, choose “Skip”.

00:00:28.549 --> 00:00:46.747
First city: Madrid. Choose country, destination, arrival date and stay length. Set the time you can start exploring. Known dates and times help build a workable route.

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:52.497
One base, several possibilities. From a city, add a day trip, continue to another destination or finish your route. A day trip fits within your stay in that city.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:01:05.582
Segovia: a day trip. Enter the place and choose a day within your stay. Add booked transport or let ITBMO organize the logistics. “No, let ITBMO handle it” means you do not need every detail now.

00:01:05.599 --> 00:01:18.682
Toledo: another experience. Add another day trip and assign it to a different available day in Madrid. You do not need transport times if they are still unknown.

00:01:18.699 --> 00:01:34.609
Next base: Barcelona. Add the next city and its dates. Day trips will fit within this new stay. Each new base can have its own day trips and connections.

00:01:34.599 --> 00:01:46.669
Connect Madrid and Barcelona. Enter the date and time you know. If transport is booked, you can add those details. Without a booking, let ITBMO organize the connection.

00:01:46.649 --> 00:01:59.732
Montserrat from Barcelona. Choose your day-trip destination and a day within the stay. Barcelona remains your base. You can also delegate the logistics for this day trip.

00:01:59.749 --> 00:02:12.832
Girona in the same trip. Repeat the process for Girona, on another available day. Keep your transport preferences. You do not need every detail resolved before continuing.

00:02:12.849 --> 00:02:28.759
A transit-only stop. If you return to Madrid to connect home, select “Transit only” instead of adding sightseeing days. Transit represents a connection, without a new sightseeing stay.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:40.819
Your return connection. Keep the Barcelona–Madrid transfer at 08:00. Review the details before saving. Logistics can remain with ITBMO if you have not booked.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:03:00.010
Your return is optional too. The origin is prefilled with your route’s last city, and you can edit it. Add the destination, date and time if known. This example: Madrid–San José at 20:00. You can also skip the return.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:07.495
Review before saving. Check cities, day trips and connections. You can edit a stop or return to the previous one before continuing. You can still correct your route.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:13.247
Confirm your route. Confirm when the details match your trip. If something is missing, return to review. Saving the route takes you to the next step.
